// Signing.xcconfig — the code-signing team, in one place.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` lived in project.pbxproj, once per
// build configuration, and flipped between two values four times in four
// months (2c73261, 2a9e8e1, e792446, 4d00217). Both values are real teams
// belonging to Isaac, and they carry names for the same person — "YITZCHAK
// ISAAC GLUCK" and "Isaac Gluck" — so Xcode's dropdown shows two entries that
// look identical while the file stores an id. Switching between them is
// invisible in the UI and silent in review.
//
// 449A45Z9N4 is the team that OWNS the app: it holds both the Development and
// the Store provisioning profile for com.IsaacGluck.baseballstats.BaseballStats.
// Its certificate is "Apple Development: YITZCHAK ISAAC GLUCK (M9326TT2DR)" —
// note that M9326TT2DR is the CERTIFICATE id; the team id is the certificate's
// OU field, which is why the id on the profile matches neither value that used
// to appear here.
//
// ⚠️ SETTING THE TEAM IN XCODE'S UI DEFEATS THIS FILE. Signing & Capabilities
// writes DEVELOPMENT_TEAM back into project.pbxproj at TARGET level, and a
// target-level setting overrides an xcconfig. That is not a reason to avoid the
// GUI — it is the reason this file is worth having: a DEVELOPMENT_TEAM line
// reappearing in the pbxproj is now a visible signal that someone touched the
// dropdown, where before it was just another line in a file nobody reads.
//
// ⚠️ SO THE INVARIANT IS: project.pbxproj contains ZERO occurrences of
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM. If `grep -c DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` on it returns anything but 0,
// this file has been silently overridden.
//
// TRACKED, DELIBERATELY. A team id is not a secret — it ships in the bundle of
// every released app. Gitignoring it would leave a fresh clone with no team, at
// which point automatic signing writes one INTO the pbxproj and the whole
// problem returns, with a clone that cannot sign on top.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = 449A45Z9N4
